# Branch Workflow

- Never commit or push directly to `main`.
- Before starting any task, run `git checkout main && git pull origin main` so you're branching from a clean, current base.
- Create a new branch for every task, named for what it does (e.g. `fix/mobile-drawer-logo`, `feat/route-scaffolding`). Never reuse an old branch name — even one that sounds related to the current task — and never commit new, unrelated work onto a branch that was already merged once.
- Commit and push all work to that new branch only.
- Once pushed, open a pull request from the branch into `main`. Report the branch name and PR link back to the user.
- Stop there. Do not merge the PR and do not push anything to `main` yourself, even if the branch builds cleanly and looks done.
- Only merge into `main` when the user explicitly says to (e.g. "merge it," "merge PR #N," "ship it to main"). This is normally after independent verification has happened outside of Cursor.
